cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "vgrav: Radial--vertical gravity decoupling in the Milky Way as a multi-model test"
version: 1.0.0
authors:
  - family-names: Monjo
    given-names: Robert
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3100-2394"
    affiliation: "CUNEF University; Universidad de Chile"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/robertmonjo/vertical_gravity"
keywords:
  - modified gravity
  - Milky Way
  - rotation curve
  - vertical potential
  - HMG
  - MOND
  - dark matter
  - reproducibility
abstract: >
  Reproducibility package for 'Radial--vertical gravity decoupling in the Milky
  Way: modified gravity and dark matter tests using Gaia DR3' (Monjo & Sasi 2026).
  Tests 12 model variants from 7 gravity frameworks (QUMOND x3, VEG x2, STVG,
  CDM NFW/Einasto, f(R) screened, Refracted Gravity, and HMG x2) against
  Wang+2026 observational data. In the best-fit baryonic configuration, HMG
  (one free parameter) leads in 62 of 100 stochastic baryonic realizations.
